  body: "# Evidence where an accident was unreported or unwitnessed\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\nThe source
    says absence of an accident record does not itself defeat a claim, while delay, explanations, consistency, corroboration
    and medical evidence may require investigation.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\nNo accident is assumed true or
    false from missing records alone. DMG 66046 continues onto the next page; the selected categories are not a
    complete evidential checklist. The project records evidence needs without collecting personal accident details.\n\
    \n## Inspected passages\n\n- [DMG 66045, PDF page 10](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a814e8b40f0b6230269697f/dmgch66.pdf#page=10).\n\
    - [DMG 66046, PDF page 10](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a814e8b40f0b6230269697f/dmgch66.pdf#page=10).\n\
    \n## Additional context\n\n- [Context: chapter 66, PDF page 11](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a814e8b40f0b6230269697f/dmgch66.pdf#page=11).\n\
    \n## Evidence and review status\n\nIndependent experimental interpretation of captured DWP guidance, not an
    official DWP document. Definitions and semantic associations are model-assisted proposals awaiting specialist
    review. No individual entitlement decision, medical conclusion, award calculation or executable rule is provided.\n\
    \nSource observation, listing-page update, printed revision, legal event and claimant-event dates are separate.
    Current legal applicability is unresolved. Page numbers are one-based PDF positions; machine extraction may
    damage reading order, characters and footnotes. No visual PDF or specialist acceptance is claimed.\n\n- `dmg-vol11-ch66`:
    PDF `8a2f49feb6557c0bc2833c308c458204e0f28cefeabbe85bc7a1ec3ae0461155`; extracted pages `a4efac777c187bd7b7d95994b53893fc4b480fe08736216f641a27ec9d6ed3d7`;
    acquired `2026-09-15T19:45:34.019999Z`.\n"
  resource: https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a814e8b40f0b6230269697f/dmgch66.pdf#page=10
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/industrial-accident-question
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The missing-record guidance concerns evidence about the occurrence and effects of the accident.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol11-ch66/0010
      quote: "66045   When considering an unreported or unwitnessed accident the DM should note that\n\n       \
        \ 1.    if notice of an accident is given and recorded by the employer soon after it\n              happened
        this is usually enough to prove a claim that there was an accident\n\n        2.    the absence of a record
        does not mean that the claim cannot succeed but\n              any long delay in reporting an accident may
        throw doubt on the claim and\n              should be carefully investigated\n\n        3.    corroboration
        by witnesses is helpful in cases where there is doubt over\n              whether an accident occurred."
      locator: DMG 66045
